  // ACTIONS" table documents `subscription.unpaid` as a distinct webhook
  // event from `subscription.cancelled` — "Downgrade to free tier, notify"
  // (day-10 of the failed-payment grace schedule) is NOT the same outcome
  // as an actual cancellation (`canceled`): the org keeps its (now free)
  // subscription and "can reactivate by updating payment method," it was
  // never told to stop. Reusing `past_due` for this state would collide two
  // genuinely different, separately-documented states into one value; a new
  // enum value is the correct fix, safe to add outright (never applied to a
  // database — see this package's DECISIONS.md header) rather than
  // reinterpreting an existing one.
  unpaid
}

